Subject: [PATCH 3/6] firmware: qcom: scm: allow QSEECOM on ASUS Vivobook S16
 S3607QA

Enables the uefisecapp client (EFI variables, efibootmgr, RTC offset).

An AI coding assistant (Anthropic Claude) drafted this change; I tested
efivars, efibootmgr and the RTC on the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DkUieTSPeVK2F2nM8a8WhL
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index b1a821d..8b5c857 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2227,6 +2227,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_qseecom_app_send);
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
+	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s16-s3607qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407na" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
